  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 48.5% accuracy while image (resnet50, singleprofile) achieves only 20.8%, suggesting the image modality is currently very weak. Uncertainty: it is unclear whether this poor image performance is due to the weak resnet50 encoder or because the image modality simply lacks discriminative signal for this task. This experiment (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) isolates the effect of image encoder quality by swapping resnet50 for a much stronger ViT-L while keeping everything else identical to config_010. Why it is the best next step: the result directly determines whether the image modality is worth pursuing at all. If ViT-L substantially improves image accuracy, multimodal fusion experiments become promising and worth the budget. If it remains poor, we can eliminate ~36 multimodal configurations and focus remaining budget on improving the RNA signal (multiprofile, better encoders). This single experiment maximally reduces strategic uncertainty before committing budget to more complex multimodal or multiprofile designs."
}

